        "date": "2026-11-12T00:37:55Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): read XZ / YZ arcs on their XY footprint in Boundary gouge law\n\nLaw (b)'s whole-move wall reading in Boundary mode judged straight moves\nand (since #905) XY arcs along their whole trace, but an XZ / YZ (G18 /\nG19) arc still answered only at its chord joints. Its XY footprint is a\nline, yet the joints stand up to a chord length apart on it: an r 200\narc's joints 1.92 mm apart read a wall vertex 3.90 mm off the footprint\n(90 um past a 4 mm cutter's floor) at >= 4.016 mm, so the gouge passed.\n\nNew sim::verify::arc_wall_plane reads a planar vertical arc as its exact\nfootprint segment (out to the coordinate's turn when the sweep passes\nit, at the radius band's outer edge) and a helical one as a bounded,\npadded polyline (at most MAX_ARC_CHORDS pieces; pad r d^2/8 plus the\nband width), so it never reads farther than the truth. Degenerate arcs\nread as the chord law cuts them; a non-finite centre fails closed.\n\nAlso from the issue: boundary_arc_walls.rs moves to crates/sim/tests\n(#921), XyArc::dist_seg uses a fixed buffer instead of a per-edge Vec,\nand a model-backed pin covers the reading with a part mesh.\n\nFixes #946\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
